  {"id":"scc-4","topic":"Spinal Cord Compression: Non-Traumatic","domain":"Internal medicine: neurology","discipline":"medicine","stem":"What anesthetic induction risk is specific to patients with traumatic or structural spinal cord injury?","answer":"Benzodiazepines, opioids, and propofol each attenuate sympathetic tone; administration may be life-threatening in patients dependent on sympathetic tone to maintain BP (neurogenic shock)","rationale":"Cord injury abolishes descending sympathetic control; any sympatholytic anesthetic may cause catastrophic hypotension.","bloom":"apply","source":[{"book":"Morgan & Mikhail","page":1350}],"confusable_with":""},
